\label{h o w(cup)}
    If $P$ and $Q$ are WQOs, then so are $P \sqcup Q$ and $P + Q$. The ordinal invariants are computed as:
    \begin{align*}
        &\textbf{h}(P \sqcup Q)=\max(\textbf{h}(P),\textbf{h}(Q))&&\textbf{h}(P+Q)=\textbf{h}(P)+\textbf{h}(Q)\\
        &\textbf{o}(P \sqcup Q)=\textbf{o}(P)\oplus\textbf{o}(Q)&&\textbf{o}(P+Q)=\textbf{o}(P)+\textbf{o}(Q)\\
        &\textbf{w}(P \sqcup Q)=\textbf{w}(P)\oplus\textbf{w}(Q)&&\textbf{w}(P+Q)=\max(\textbf{w}(P),\textbf{w}(Q))
    \end{align*}

\label{h o(times)}
    If $P$ and $Q$ are WQOs, then so is $P \times Q$. The height and maximal order type are computed as:
    \begin{align*}
        &\textbf{h}(P \times Q) = \sup_{\alpha < \textbf{h}(P), \beta < \textbf{h}(Q)} \alpha\oplus\beta+1\\
        &\textbf{o}(P \times Q) = \textbf{o}(P) \otimes \textbf{o}(Q)
    \end{align*}

