\label{w rec tree}
    Let $Q$ be an initial segment of a WQO $Q'$, and let $a \in Q' \setminus Q$. For a set of trees $X \subset \mathcal{T}(Q')$, we define $\mathcal{T}(Q, a, X)$ to be the set of those $Q'$-labeled trees that have the following properties:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item The tree has at least one vertex labeled with $a$.
        \item If all ascendants of some vertex have labels from $Q$, then the vertex has a label from $Q \cup \{a\}$.
        \item If, in addition, that vertex has a label $a$, then it is not a leaf, and all its immediate descendants' subtrees are in $X$.
    \end{enumerate}

The first claim immediately follows from \cref{embedding}. For the second claim, consider a reflection $F \mapsto rF$ from $\mathsf{P_f^{2}}(\mathcal{T}^{
leqslant r}(Q, a, X))$ to $\mathcal{T}^Q(Q, a, X)$. By \cref{w(S2),embedding}, $	extbf{w}(\mathcal{T}^Q(Q, a, X)) \geqslant 	extbf{w}(\mathsf{P_f^{2}}(\mathcal{T}^{
leqslant r}(Q, a, X))) \geqslant 	extbf{w}(\mathcal{T}^{
leqslant r}(Q, a, X))$.

Let $s \in Q$ be incomparable with $r$. We have the reflections $\mathsf{P_f^{2}}(\mathcal{T}^{
leqslant r}(Q, a, X)) \hookrightarrow \mathcal{T}^r(Q, a, X)$ and $\mathcal{T}^r(Q, a, X) \hookrightarrow \mathcal{T}^{
leqslant r}(Q, a, X)$ given by $F \mapsto rF$ and $t \mapsto st$, respectively. By \cref{embedding}, $	extbf{w}(\mathcal{T}^{
leqslant r}(Q, a, X)) \geqslant 	extbf{w}(\mathcal{T}^r(Q, a, X)) \geqslant 	extbf{w}(\mathsf{P_f^{2}}(\mathcal{T}^{
leqslant r}(Q, a, X)))$. If $	extbf{w}(\mathcal{T}^{
leqslant r}(Q, a, X))$ is finite, then it is at least 4 and $	extbf{w}(\mathsf{P_f^{2}}(\mathcal{T}^{
leqslant r}(Q, a, X))) > 	extbf{w}(\mathcal{T}^{
leqslant r}(Q, a, X))$, a contradiction. Hence, it is infinite and $	extbf{w}(\mathcal{T}^{
leqslant r}(Q, a, X)) = 	extbf{w}(\mathcal{T}^r(Q, a, X)) =2^{	extbf{w}(\mathcal{T}^{
leqslant r}(Q, a, X))}$, which proves the claim.

